<title>USA: IPO PRICING - Ingram Micro at $18 a share.</title>
<headline>IPO PRICING - Ingram Micro at $18 a share.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Ingram Micro Inc were priced at $18 each for the computer distribution powerhouse's initial public offering tomorrow, according to lead underwriter Morgan Stanley.</p>
<p>The shares priced at the middle of the estimated pricing range of $17 to $19. That range had been revised higher due to heavy demand from an initial range of $14 to $16 a share.</p>
<p>The company is offering 20 million shares, making the deal worth $360 million. Analysts say they expect the deal to garner strong premiums at its market debut.</p>
</text>
